## Reading
All eleven statements elaborate at the issue commit (only `exact?` reports errors), so the ladder statements of the
brief are well typed. Results: L4 (exists_colSimRed_fixCoins), L7a (negligible ε), L7b (K ≤ |x|²): no closing term.
L7 (col_zk): only the sorried target. L1, L2, L3, L5a, L5b, L5c, L6: `exact?` timed out at 400000 heartbeats
(inconclusive); the name/statement greps find no equivalent public lemma (no `statClose_sampleColorPair`; nothing on
`colRealView` or `colSimTrunc` beyond Claim-129.a/c; the only two-parameter coin transport is
`LevinTransfer.distinguisherL_lift`, specific to `postView` and truncated coins; the only verifier-call polytime lemma is
`ColSimMachine.reply_poly`, whose tape is `rVStr ℓ x blk`). The machine L5 itself (`exists_colHidingRed`) needs a new
string function and is stated in the brief by interface only.
